In `libqtile/scripts/top.py`, `get_stats` computes `total` with `sum(stat.size for stat in top_stats)`. In the QA test file, `get_trace` is monkeypatched to return a `_DummySnapshot(stats)`, `filter_snapshot` is monkeypatched to return the snapshot unchanged, and `_DummySnapshot.statistics()` returns that same stats list, so `top_stats` is exactly the list built by `_build_case_stats(case_id)`. Thus, for each of the 15 parametrized `case_id` values, `total` is the sum of the generated `size` fields for that case; taking the minimum and maximum of those 15 sums yields 7612 and 28886.

## Answer
{"variable":"total","min_value":7612,"max_value":28886}
